    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d352">

                <pb facs="0559" n="463" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg463"/>

                <head>No. 352.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Mr. Riotte.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-02-22"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 22,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 68.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>. Referring to your dispatch No. 97, of the
                    21st ultimo, on the subject of the exploration of the Nicaraguan Isthmus, with a
                    view to the construction of an interoceanic canal, I have to inform you that an
                    expedition for that purpose has been ordered by this Government, and that a
                    vessel may be expected in Nicaragua in a few weeks, to begin the survey. I take
                    this occasion to acknowledge the receipt of your dispatch No. 96, of the 11th
                    ultimo.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
